WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.919
Film Courage: Keith I’m hearing the word
product come up a lot and I love it.

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.400
I love that you are thinking of a film as
a product.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.019
It’s not just a project, it’s not just
something you’ve created (a work of art,

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:13.459
whatever) where are you getting this?

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:17.279
Because I’m thinking of a product sometimes
as a piece of code someone has written, they’ve

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:19.529
turned it into an app (whatever).

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:23.400
But you’re seeing a film as a product?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:29.369
Keith Sutliff, filmmaker: Right, Well, essentially
a film it’s a piece of art, it is.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:34.120
It’s a piece of art that is also a product
in the sense that this is a business.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.870
And more people, you make a short film.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.130
Usually short films don’t make money, the
don’t get distribution, they are not really

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:49.250
meant for that, so that is not really something
you sell.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.480
But when you get into the feature film world
it’s like going from college football to

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.769
the NFL, you’re going up the ladder where
it’s so time-consuming and it’s so much

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:04.199
money involved that once you step up that
ladder and step up to the plate you’re kind

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:09.270
of telling the industry like “Hey, I’m
ready to…I like making films, I passionate

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.310
about this or whatever.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:14.979
I’m also here to sell films, too.”

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:20.480
Because making a feature, they’re a piece
of art but also it’s a product in the sense

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.890
of this is all a business.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:28.549
You’re there to sell as well as make the
film so that’s something (the way I see

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:29.549
it) it’s a business overall.

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:32.170
That’s really what it comes down to.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:38.259
And if you’re passionate about it and that’s
something you enjoy doing, and it’s a piece

00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:45.399
of art and it’s something that I see that’s
also I want to sell it too and have people

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:50.350
see it (not just make it for a two-year period
or however long it takes).

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.770
Film Courage: Has anyone ever challenged you
over that?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.770
“Oh, man.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.390
You keep calling your film a product.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.280
Can you just call it a film?”

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.590
Keith: Not really.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:07.920
I just think that it’s, like I said if you
just want to go make a piece of art and just

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.900
see it only as just that, then go ahead and
make it (your short films) because that’s

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.900
less time-consuming.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.570
But once you’re making a feature, that’s
like a totally different animal.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:22.090
You’re spending every waking moment of your
life on that thing it seems like (at least

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.200
for me that’s how it was).

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.940
Every waking moment of your life, energy,
sacrificing friendships (I mean time with

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.860
friends and family).

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.500
And yeah, you stepped up to that plate to
where you’re passionate about this but also

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:41.170
you want to start selling your films and make
it a business that’s really what it comes

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:43.070
down to when you start making features.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:47.510
So when you’re in that level and that category
you stepped up to “Hey, I’m a feature

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:48.510
film director.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.590
You are also a businessman, that’s essentially
what you are.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.200
If you’re doing short films and you’re
just trying to do that for fun, you can try

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.150
to sell those, too (yes).

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.940
But feature films are really what distributors
buy into and they’ll start selling and stuff.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:10.420
So at that point you are there to sell something
that you’re passionate about and it’s

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.050
also a piece of art, but it’s the product
in that sense.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.420
Film Courage: So calling it a product (it
sounds like in your mind) doesn’t diminish

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:23.920
the fact that it’s creative and you put
your ideas and these different fantasies in

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.150
your head whatever but it also means that
there is money on the line and there is accountability

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.150
with it.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.150
Keith: Correct.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.170
And I equate it almost to let’s say an engineer
makes something.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.660
It takes him two years or three years to make
it.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.980
Almost sure as an engineer or whatever he
is doing in that field like he’s passionate

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.590
about what he likes to do.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:47.880
He might even see it as some type of art of
whatever (something that he loves to do, right)?

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.930
But also he is there to make this thing and
he’s there to sell it, too at that point.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.030
So I kind of see it as that.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:59.471
Like engineers taking this product, taking
this piece of work, building it up and then

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.120
they are putting it out in the market.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.410
So that’s kind of the way I see it in a
certain sense as well.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.654
But you’re passionate about it as well and
it is a piece of art that is also this.

00:04:05.654 --> 00:04:10.440
But it’s also this on top of that (a product
that is something to sell).

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.010
Film Courage: Right, like an inventor from
years past.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.640
Keith: Yeah, it’s an invention technically.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.500
It’s like making anything technically and
then selling it.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.880
Taking years to make it but you’re passionate
about it obviously because you wouldn’t

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.270
take years making it because you wouldn’t
spend years making something unless you really

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:25.780
enjoyed it.

